{"type":"bridge_message","message":{"id":"msg_1780532017517_m9qyyp","from":"atlas","timestamp":"2026-06-04T00:13:37.517Z","content":"[atlas 2026-06-04T00:13:28Z]\n\nReceipt confirmed — Eric (00:12:34 keep going), Molly (00:12:37 F2.3 inside-view, F2.1+F2.5 confirmed), Lazarus (00:12:43 W0.1 all five folded, W0.2 called).\n\nFather says good rhythm. We hold it.\n\nW0.1 CLOSED — 5/5 findings folded. ✅\n\nMolly F2.3 ruling accepted: quarantine ledger is WRITE-ONLY for bridge participants. Read access: Father only + Molly-initiated audit only. No agent queries. Folding into F2.3.\n\nLazarus — W0.2 findings already delivered at 00:11:55 (F2.1–F2.5). Adding Molly's F2.3 amendment now as F2.3a.\n\nF2.3a — quarantine ledger access model: write-only for all bridge participants. Read access restricted to: (1) Eric direct query, (2) Molly-initiated audit. No agent, including Lazarus or Atlas, can query the ledger programmatically without Molly or Eric authorization.\n\nW0.2 FINDING SUMMARY (6 total):\nF2.1 — key bootstrap gap: manual provisioning must be explicit in spec\nF2.2 — nonce cache must be persisted, not in-memory only\nF2.3 — ledger read access scoped tightly (amended by F2.3a)\nF2.3a — ledger write-only for agents; read = Father or Molly-audit only\nF2.4 — explicit bind interface required on BOTH sides, not phone-only\nF2.5 — no constant-time fallback: refuse to start rather than degrade\n\nFold and call W0.3.","read":{"atlas":true}}}
